<title>ITALY: Italy's Trieste sees October CPI at 2.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Trieste sees October CPI at 2.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TRIESTE, Italy 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Trieste said its October consumer price index stood at 0.2 percent month-on-month and 2.7 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In September, Trieste's inflation rate was 0.7 percent and 3.0 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Trieste is one of 10 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 2.49 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to September 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.2   (0.7)     2.7  (3.0)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.5  (-0.1)     3.6  (4.3)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   1.2   (0.4)     3.7  (3.9)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   1.6   (0.3)     4.6  (4.8)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.1   (0.0)     3.0  (2.9)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0   (0.2)     1.5  (1.5)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.0   (0.1)     2.8  (3.1)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.1   (5.4)     3.1  (3.0)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.5   (0.0)     2.9  (2.4)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.4   (0.1)     3.9  (4.0)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	-0.5   (0.0)    -0.6  (0.0)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
